  "body": "The [section on scripting languages](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#scriptingLanguages) currently says:\r\n\r\n> For external JavaScript resources, MIME type parameters in `Content-Type` headers are generally ignored. (In some cases the `charset` parameter has an effect.) However, for the script element's type attribute they are significant; it uses the JavaScript MIME type essence match concept.\r\n\r\nIt seems like this is a bit out of date given that [the rules for fetching module scripts](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#fetch-a-single-module-script) specify (in step 8) that MIME type checking *is* performed for module scripts.\r\n\r\nIt seems like this quoted paragraph should be updated to reflect the new behavior for module scripts.",
